  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 108 PM CDT Sun Aug 23 2026\n\nBy Wednesday the large 500 MB heat dome will remain in place\nover the southwestern/south central CONUS, while the trough\ndescribed in the SHORT TERM section above moves away to our\neast. This will allow deep-layer ridging to reassert itself just\nto our west, leading to a period of dry, quiet, and seasonally\nmild weather with daily highs in the low to mid-80s for the\nremainder of the week. By Friday and Saturday the pattern will\nbegin to shift a bit, as two large 500 MB lows develop over\nCanada and shunt the ridge southward, with the heat dome\nretrograding more over the far southwestern CONUS near Arizona\nand New Mexico. This will cause 500 MB flow over Iowa to become\nmore zonal, with multiple shortwave impulses moving through the\nflow and providing several opportunities for thunderstorms from\nFriday or Saturday into early the following week. While the\ndetails of any such storms are very uncertain at this range, it\nis fair to say that overall the weather pattern will be more\nactive by next weekend.",
